1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,730
Two billion years ago, Earth built its own working nuclear reactor.

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:09,480
In Oklo, Gabon, underground water met highly enriched natural uranium ores.

3
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:13,560
Water slowed down neutrons, triggering a sustained nuclear chain reaction.

4
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:17,750
Pause—how did this natural power plant avoid blowing itself apart?

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,570
It built a self-regulating safety system without human control.

6
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:25,380
Heat boiled away water, stopping fission until it cooled.

7
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:29,190
This alien engine ran for one hundred thousand years.

8
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:33,380
Modern scientists still cannot match its perfect nuclear waste containment.

9
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,710
Long before humans existed,
